Newspeak3
'Root'
class BuildInfo packageUsing: manifest = Object new (
	(* Provenance of the sources this image was built from. This committed copy
	is a placeholder; tool/build.sh generates the real one into out/ at build
	time (step 7c), so a built image reports its true provenance while the
	working tree is left untouched. Do not commit a generated copy.

	`version` and `dirty` describe the SOURCES, so every artifact built from
	them shares these correctly. `builtAt` is when the artifact was built, and
	is reached through `platform buildTime` -- the platform's enclosing runtime
	holds whichever BuildInfo it was packaged with, so a deployment generated
	later than the image that produced it can report its own date instead of
	inheriting that image's.

	Best-effort about one thing none of this can see: the IDE can change its
	own source at any time, so an image may be running code matching no commit.
	The sha says what it was BUILT from, not what it is now. *)
	
) (
) : (
	public builtAt = (
		^'unknown'
	)
	public dirty = (
		^''
	)
	public version = (
		^'development build'
	)
)
